.\"                                      Hey, EMACS: -*- nroff -*-
.TH GOBLIN-MOSH-COMPILE-DICTIONARY 1 "May 2026"
.SH NAME
goblin-mosh-compile-dictionary \- build a zstd dictionary for Mosh state updates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B goblin-mosh-compile-dictionary
\-\-input=\fIFILE\fP
\-\-output=\fIFILE\fP
[\-\-dict-size=\fIBYTES\fP]
[\-\-max-samples=\fIN\fP]
.br
.B goblin-mosh-compile-dictionary
[\fIoptions\fP]
\fIINPUT\fP
\fIOUTPUT\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgoblin-mosh-compile-dictionary\fP reads a Mosh state sample log produced by
\fBgoblin-mosh --state-sample-log\fP and trains a zstd dictionary for later
terminal state compression. The output dictionary file is compressed
with zstd level 22.

The sample log contains received, uncompressed terminal state blobs in
a zstd-compressed framed format. It can include terminal contents and
should be treated as sensitive.

Use the generated dictionary with
.BR "goblin-mosh --state-zstd-dict=" "FILE" .
The wrapper uploads the dictionary over SSH during setup, and the
server decompresses it and uses it for that Mosh session only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-input=\fIFILE\fP
Read samples from \fIFILE\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-output=\fIFILE\fP
Write the compiled dictionary to \fIFILE\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-dict\-size=\fIBYTES\fP
Maximum dictionary size. The default is 65536 bytes.
.TP
.B \-\-max\-samples=\fIN\fP
Train from at most \fIN\fP samples. The default, 0, means all samples.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
$ goblin-mosh --state-sample-log=emacs.samples.zst host
$ goblin-mosh-compile-dictionary --input=emacs.samples.zst --output=emacs.dict
$ goblin-mosh --state-zstd-dict=emacs.dict host
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR goblin-mosh (1),
.BR goblin-mosh-client (1),
.BR goblin-mosh-server (1).
